  "source": "The Swedish Council for Information on Alcohol and Other Drugs (CAN)",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: Percentage (%) of pupils in school year 9 that state that they have consumed alcohol or got drunk at the age of 13 or younger. Question: 'How old were you when you (if ever) did the following things [drank at least one glass of alcohol]/[got drunk] the first time?' The indicator refers to the percentage that replied '11 years or younger', '12 years' or '13 years'."
  ]
